+## Build with GitHub Actions
+
+The repository includes `.github/workflows/build-demo-ipa.yml`. It uses the
+official `macos-26` GitHub-hosted runner, selects Xcode 26.2, builds the
+`release_arm64` device target with Telegram's checked-in fake signing data, and
+uploads `TelegramDemo.ipa` as the `TelegramDemo-IPA` workflow artifact.
+
+1. Push the patched source to a GitHub fork.
+2. Open **Actions → Build Demo IPA → Run workflow**.
+3. Download the `TelegramDemo-IPA` artifact when the job finishes.
+4. Unzip it and install `TelegramDemo.ipa` with Sideloadly. Sideloadly replaces
+   the fake signature with a signature for your Apple ID during installation.
+
+This workflow intentionally runs only by manual dispatch because a clean
+Telegram iOS build is large. GitHub's checked-in `appstore-configuration.json`
+is used only to satisfy the upstream build system. Demo Mode itself stays
+offline. If you distribute a build or enable real-account login for other
+people, replace the API and branding configuration with your own values as
+required by the upstream README.
+
 The demo number is intercepted before `auth.sendCode`, and the demo code is
 validated locally before any request reaches Telegram.
